{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaHabiroGeneratorRigidity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaHabiroGeneratorRigidity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.GroupWithZero.Units.Basic"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.FixedTwoTermGeneratorConjecture","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.FixedTwoTermGeneratorConjecture","kind":"def","line":312,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaHabiroGeneratorRigidity.lean#L312-L320","doc":"**The sole open input** for the two-pole route, recorded as a *defined, not\nasserted* predicate (§3b-tax primary conjecture; no instance, no proof): that the\nladder tower `c` admits a fixed two-term rational generator whose denominator\ncarries the proved `c_2 = -1` anchor `Q₂ = Q₀`. That the transcendental on-`main`\ngenerator `cos(Φ(u))` realizes such a rational element reproducing production\n`Q_β` at `q_0` is the open kernel frontier — this derives the rigidity that\n*would* follow, never that the generator exists. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.two_term_generator_rigid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.two_term_generator_rigid","kind":"theorem","line":301,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaHabiroGeneratorRigidity.lean#L301-L310","doc":"**Generator rigidity — fixing `(P,Q)` removes all freedom.** Two coefficient\ntowers `c, c'` arising from the *same* fixed two-term generator `(P,Q)` are equal.\nThe formal content of \"you cannot re-choose `c_3` once the categorical generator\nis fixed\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.c2_eq_neg_one_of_anchor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.c2_eq_neg_one_of_anchor","kind":"theorem","line":288,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaHabiroGeneratorRigidity.lean#L288-L299","doc":"The **proved** rung falls out. With the anchor `Q₂ = Q₀` (encoding the\nTaylor-exact `a_2 = c_2 = -1` kernel rung) and the ladder seed `c_0 = 1, c_1 = 0`,\nthe fixed generator recovers `c_2 = -1`. `c_3` is *not* recovered — it needs\n`Q₁`, the open bar-odd datum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.c3_not_free","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.c3_not_free","kind":"theorem","line":281,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaHabiroGeneratorRigidity.lean#L281-L286","doc":"**The anti-flip-flop crux.** Once the generator `(P,Q)` is fixed, `c_3` obeys\n`Q₀·c_3 + Q₁·c_2 + Q₂·c_1 = 0` — a *dependent* quantity tied to `c_1, c_2` and the\nfixed generator, **not** a free per-session fit. No `c_3` value is asserted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.two_term_tail_recurrence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.two_term_tail_recurrence","kind":"theorem","line":270,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaHabiroGeneratorRigidity.lean#L270-L279","doc":"**A fixed two-term generator forces the depth-2 recurrence.** For every\n`n ≥ 2`, `Q₀·c_n + Q₁·c_{n-1} + Q₂·c_{n-2} = 0`. The recurrence is a\n*consequence* of rationality, not the on-`main` ansatz. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.tail_recurrence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.tail_recurrence","kind":"theorem","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaHabiroGeneratorRigidity.lean#L252-L267","doc":"General tail recurrence: with numerator degree `≤ dP` and denominator degree\n`≤ dQ`, the coefficients satisfy `∑_{j≤dQ} Q_j · c_{n-j} = 0` for every `n > dP`\nwith `n ≥ dQ`. The extra high-`j` terms vanish by `Q j = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IsTwoTermGenerator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IsTwoTermGenerator","kind":"def","line":244,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaHabiroGeneratorRigidity.lean#L244-L249","doc":"`c` is generated by a **fixed two-term rational element** `P / Q`:\ndenominator degree `≤ 2` (two-term, the `[2]_q`-shape), numerator degree `≤ 1`,\nand `Q 0` a unit. A *property* of `(c, P, Q)`; no `c_k` value is fixed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.conv_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.conv_unique","kind":"theorem","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaHabiroGeneratorRigidity.lean#L222-L242","doc":"**Uniqueness of the holonomic tower.** If `Q 0` is a unit, the convolution\nequation `Q * c = Q * c'` (both sides the same numerator `P`) forces `c = c'`.\nStrong induction: peeling the `j = 0` term isolates `Q₀·c_n`; every other term\nreferences a strictly smaller index handled by the hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.convCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.convCoeff","kind":"def","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaHabiroGeneratorRigidity.lean#L216-L219","doc":"The Cauchy product `(Q * c)_n = ∑_{j≤n} Q_j · c_{n-j}` — the coefficient-level\nmeaning of the rational generating function `c = P / Q`, i.e. `P = Q * c`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qbeta_ladder_rigid_of_single_generator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qbeta_ladder_rigid_of_single_generator","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaHabiroGeneratorRigidity.lean#L193-L205","doc":"**Conditional rigidity (§3b-cond).** GIVEN the open single-generator\nclass, the `2×2` Hankel / Casoratian minor of the true tower vanishes —\n`c 2 · c 4 = c 3²` — so every rung `k ≥ 4` is forced by `c 2` and\n`c 3`. Proved sorry-free FROM the class; derives no `c_k` value. This\nis the honest statement \"fixing the generator eliminates the\nflip-flop\": the per-rung classes of `QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder`\nwould all collapse into the two parameters `(ρ, c 2)` of one fixed\nelement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaSingleHabiroGenerator.exists_single_generator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaSingleHabiroGenerator.exists_single_generator","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaHabiroGeneratorRigidity.lean#L191-L191","doc":"The tower is rank-1: some fixed ratio `ρ` governs every rung `k ≥ 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaSingleHabiroGenerator.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaSingleHabiroGenerator.mk","kind":"ctor","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaHabiroGeneratorRigidity.lean#L189-L189","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaSingleHabiroGenerator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaSingleHabiroGenerator","kind":"class","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaHabiroGeneratorRigidity.lean#L174-L191","doc":"**OPEN: the Q_β tower is a single fixed bar-odd Habiro generator.**\n\nContent-bearing conjecture class (§3b). It asserts that the TRUE\ncategorical tower coefficients `cTrue` come from ONE fixed generator —\ni.e. there is a ratio `ρ` for which the rank-1 / Casoratian law holds\nat every rung `k ≥ 2`. The intended `ρ` is the categorical bar-odd\n(\"sinh partner\") Habiro element dual to the bar-even `[2]_q` prefactor\nof α_EM (cf. `QBetaResidueHabiroDual`), whose existence is the open\ntarget `probe-qbeta-habiro-element-search`.\n\n**No instance is provided** — the open state is the absence of a proof\nterm. The class asserts NOTHING about the VALUE of any `c_k` (in\nparticular nothing about `c_3`); it asserts only that fixing the\ngenerator removes the per-rung freedom. Producing an instance would\nrequire deriving the generator, which is NOT done here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.not_single_generator_of_hankel_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.not_single_generator_of_hankel_ne","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaHabiroGeneratorRigidity.lean#L149-L158","doc":"**Flip-flop obstruction (contrapositive).** A non-vanishing Hankel\nminor `c 2 · c 4 ≠ c 3²` certifies that NO single-generator ratio `ρ`\nreproduces the tower — the coefficients carry genuine per-rung freedom\nbeyond a single fixed generator. This is the precise, checkable sense\nin which an independently-fitted `c_k` menu \"can flip-flop\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hankel_minor_vanishes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hankel_minor_vanishes","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaHabiroGeneratorRigidity.lean#L132-L147","doc":"**Rank-1 / Casoratian minor vanishes.** Under the single-generator\nlaw the `2×2` Hankel minor of `(c 2, c 3, c 4)` is zero:\n\n  `c 2 · c 4 = c 3 ²`.\n\nThis is the coefficient-sequence Casoratian — the bar-odd mirror of\n`HabiroNewtonLadder.casoratian_eq_zero` (which collapses the bar-even\n4₁ Newton-node Casoratian). It is the single checkable equation that\n\"the tower comes from one fixed generator\" imposes on the first three\nlive rungs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.single_generator_forces","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.single_generator_forces","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaHabiroGeneratorRigidity.lean#L115-L130","doc":"**Every higher rung is forced by `(ρ, c 2)`.** Under the single-\ngenerator law, `c (k+2) = ρ^k · c 2` for all `k`. So a single fixed\ngenerator has exactly **two** free parameters (`ρ` and `c 2`); once\n`c 2` and `c 3` are known, `ρ` is pinned (`ρ = c 3 / c 2` over a\nfield) and every rung `k ≥ 4` is determined — no independent\nper-rung freedom survives. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SingleGeneratorLaw","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SingleGeneratorLaw","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaHabiroGeneratorRigidity.lean#L102-L113","doc":"A **single-generator (rank-1) coefficient law** for a ladder\ncoefficient sequence `c : ℕ → K`: from index `2` on, consecutive\ncoefficients are in fixed ratio `ρ`,\n\n  `c (k+1) = ρ · c k`   for all `k ≥ 2`.\n\nThis is the hallmark of ONE fixed simple generator `1/(1 − ρu)`\n(a single pole), as opposed to independently chosen per-rung\ncoefficients `c_2, c_3, c_4, …` — the current corpus situation, in\nwhich each `c_k` lives behind its own conditional class. ","signatureChunk":0}]}